      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Loki entró y todos callaron. Pidió una silla, y Odín, que había jurado hermandad de sangre con él, se la concedió.",
          "en": "Loki walked in and everyone fell silent. He asked for a seat, and Odin, who had once sworn blood-brotherhood with him, allowed it."
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces acusó a los dioses, uno por uno. A Odín le reprochó que daba la victoria a los cobardes.",
          "en": "Then he began to accuse the gods, one by one. He told Odin that he gave victory to cowards."
        },
        {
          "es": "Frigg le dijo que, si Baldr estuviera allí, Loki no saldría vivo del salón.",
          "en": "Frigg told him that if Baldr were there, Loki would not leave the hall alive."
        },
        {
          "es": "Y Loki respondió, sin vergüenza, que él era la razón por la que Baldr jamás volvería a entrar a ese salón.",
          "en": "And Loki answered, shamelessly, that he was the reason Baldr would never walk into that hall again."
        },
        {
          "es": "A Freyja le dijo que había tenido demasiados amantes. Ella solo contestó que Loki estaba loco por hablar así.",
          "en": "He told Freyja she had taken too many lovers. She only replied that Loki was mad to speak that way."
        }
      ],
