          1.08
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "A Tyr le recordó su mano perdida. Tyr contestó que Loki había perdido a su hijo Fenrir, atado hasta el fin del mundo.",
          "en": "He reminded Tyr of his lost hand. Tyr replied that Loki had lost his own son Fenrir, bound until the end of the world."
        },
        {
          "es": "A Njord le recordó que había llegado a Asgard como rehén de los vanir.",
          "en": "He told Njord that he had come to Asgard as a hostage of the Vanir."
        },
        {
          "es": "A Heimdall le dijo que su destino era vigilar siempre, con la espalda mojada, sin descansar jamás.",
          "en": "He told Heimdall that his fate was to keep watch forever, with a wet back, never resting."
        },
        {
          "es": "Sif le ofreció una copa de hidromiel para calmarlo. Él la bebió, pero no dejó de burlarse.",
          "en": "Sif offered him a cup of mead to calm him. He drank it, but he did not stop mocking them."
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces Skadi le advirtió que un día los dioses lo atarían con las entrañas de su propio hijo.",
          "en": "Then Skadi warned him that one day the gods would bind him with the entrails of his own son."
        }
