      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Los dioses lo llevaron a una cueva y levantaron tres losas de piedra, cada una con un agujero.",
          "en": "The gods took him to a cave and raised three flat stones, each with a hole in it."
        },
        {
          "es": "Convirtieron a Vali, hijo de Loki, en lobo, y Vali atacó a su hermano Narfi, que murió.",
          "en": "They turned Vali, a son of Loki, into a wolf, and he attacked his brother Narfi, who died."
        },
        {
          "es": "Con las entrañas de Narfi ataron a Loki sobre las tres piedras: bajo los hombros, la cintura y las rodillas.",
          "en": "With Narfi's entrails the gods bound Loki across the three stones: under his shoulders, his waist and his knees."
        },
        {
          "es": "En cuanto lo ataron, las tiras se volvieron hierro, y nadie pudo romperlas jamás.",
          "en": "The moment he was bound, the cords turned to iron, and no one could ever break them."
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces Skadi colgó una serpiente venenosa sobre su cara, para que el veneno le cayera gota a gota.",
          "en": "Then Skadi hung a venomous snake above his face, so that its venom would fall drop by drop."
